; A call through a far function pointer (small memory model): the compiler
; puts the pointer in R4 (segment offset) and R5 (segment) and CALLS this,
; which jumps to the function with the caller's return address still on
; the system stack, so the function returns straight to the caller. The
; stock 5WY19 firmware does the same at 2000H. Hand-written; part of
; openc166 (MIT).

$NOMACRO
$CASE
$MOD167
$SEGMENTED

ICALL_PR        SECTION CODE WORD PUBLIC 'CPROGRAM'
        PUBLIC  ___c166_icall
___c166_icall   PROC    FAR
        PUSH    R5
        PUSH    R4
        RETS
___c166_icall   ENDP
ICALL_PR        ENDS
        END
